  "decision": {
    "answer": "SUPPORTS",
    "explanation": "The evidence from pmid-9839497 explicitly states that patients with the RET M918T mutation (associated with the MEN 2B subtype) developed 'larger and more aggressive medullary thyroid cancer compared to other genotypes'. This directly supports the claim that the RET M918T variant in Medullary Thyroid Carcinoma is associated with a poor outcome. The evidence confirms the molecular profile (RET M918T), the disease (Medullary Thyroid Carcinoma), and the prognostic significance (aggressive/larger tumors implying poor outcome). The variant origin is described as germline (MEN 2B subtype involves germline mutations), aligning with the RARE_GERMLINE aspect of the claim.",
    "citations": [
      {
        "document_id": "pmid-9839497",
        "start": 0,
        "end": 269,
        "quote": "In a study of 64 patients (48 kindreds), 62 had germline mutations at known hotspots in RET. Patients with RET M918T mutation were associated with MEN 2B subtype and developed larger and more aggressive medullary thyroid cancer compared to other genotypes (e.g. C618S)."
      }
    ],
